{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1413297-unique-powers","id":1413297,"title":"unique powers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-12T17:04:14-07:00","id":1413297,"title":"unique powers","content":"Japhet's character sheet says he has a plethora of powers, many of which are unique to them. Are any of these unique powers known? And i am not just talking about Japhet. Are there other vampires in the lore who have been known to have powers exclusive to them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-12T23:51:00-07:00","id":1413335,"title":"","content":"They are not known. Presumably they're his elder Disciplines, though they could just as easily also include some other totally unique non-Discipline powers. Inyanga was able to turn into a leopard through a non-Protean mystic ritual. The Three (Nosferatu mortal triplets from Constantinople by Night) could telepathically communicate with each other across the city. It's a big World of Darkness. Don't feel limited by the standard Discipline powers in the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T00:03:30-07:00","id":1413337,"title":"","content":"Many elders especially Methuselahs may have a lot of unique powers. It is very likely that Ur-Shulgi knows many ancient and forgotten rituals and you will never live to see them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T00:11:03-07:00","id":1413338,"title":"","content":"Since no time is actually taken to <b>describe</b> any such unique powers - and consequently, their utter irrelevance to the actual story/adventure where the sheet was published - it's quite safe to assume the writer meant a generic/standard bunch elder powers for the sake of snowflakeness &quot;see how this NPC we half-@$$ed at writing is awesome by numbers&quot;.... -__-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T02:38:21-07:00","id":1413353,"title":"","content":"There are some vampires with interesting combo disciplines. <br /> <br /> Some thinbloods develop special disciplines, but those are mostly Protean variants i think. <br /> <br /> you could always think up a Thaumaturgy path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T07:58:55-07:00","id":1413373,"title":"","content":"Anyway, if we are speaking of Japheth's &quot;sheet&quot; in Last Supper, i would say those stats have very debatable canonicity, having been written with apparently little to no awareness of what the Cappadocians would turn into (Auspex 8 ok, Dominate 8 &amp; Thaumaturgy 9.... eh?). I would suggest moving around some of his displines and the atribute priorization (physicals almost as high as the mental doesn't really mesh with his skillset, self-control 4 in someone <i>that lets itself be diablerized</i>, even less so) if one does intend to use that as reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-13-2020, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T12:16:12-07:00","id":1413412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1413297-unique-powers?p=1413353#post1413353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some vampires with interesting combo disciplines.<br /> <br /> Some thinbloods develop special disciplines, but those are mostly Protean variants i think.<br /> <br /> you could always think up a Thaumaturgy path.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Didn't Lazarus have a serpentis/necromancy combo unique to him? He turned into a monstrous jackal or something","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}